# Nail Feed — Content Authoring & Component Reference

Route: `/nail-feed` (hyphenated URL; files/folders internally use `nailfeed`,
no hyphen — this split is intentional, not a bug).

This README covers **everything** needed to write a Nail Feed post and
understand how the page renders it: every frontmatter field, every widget,
where things appear on the page, and what happens if a field is missing.

---

## 1. Quick Start — Minimal Post

```yaml
---
title: "Your Post Title"
excerpt: "One-sentence summary shown in listings and social previews."
date: "2026-08-08"
author: "jyoti-mirelle"
category: "Trends"
image: "/images/nailfeed/your-image.jpg"
imageAlt: "Descriptive alt text"
imageWidth: 1200
imageHeight: 675
readTime: "3 min"
topic: "your-topic-slug"
canonical: "https://mirelleinspo.com/nail-feed/your-slug"
---

## Your First Section

Body content here.

## Your Second Section

More content.
```

This alone is a valid, publishable post. Everything else in this file is
optional enhancement.

**Author field takes several accepted formats** — recommend the slug
(`"ri-mirelle"` / `"jyoti-mirelle"`) for consistency — see [Author
Matching](#7-author-matching) for why.

