## 5. `topicalMap` — SEO/Content Cluster Metadata

**Trimmed shape** — only 5 fields (deliberately cut from /blog's fuller
version; the cut fields have zero application-code consumers, confirmed via
grep). Don't add the cut fields back without a real, named reason.

```yaml
topicalMap:
  parentPillar: "/blog/your-pillar-page"
  relatedClusters:
    - "related-cluster-slug"
  primaryKeyword: "main target keyword"
  secondaryKeywords:
    - "secondary keyword one"
    - "secondary keyword two"
  topicalBoundary: "One sentence describing what this post does/doesn't cover"
```

This is metadata for the content funnel model (Nail Feed spokes link back
to /blog pillars via `parentPillar`) — not currently read by any rendering
logic, purely organizational/for future tooling.

