## 6. Engagement Widgets

Three optional widgets: **Reaction Bar**, **Poll**, **Quiz**. All three are
controlled entirely through frontmatter — no code changes needed to author
new instances of any of them. Visual design (colors, borders, animation) is
fixed in the components; frontmatter only controls text content and (for
quiz) scoring logic.

### 6.1 Reaction Bar

**Always renders on every post — even with zero `reaction` frontmatter.**
There is no "off" state. If you don't write a `reaction` block, it falls
back to a hardcoded default:

```
✨ Obsessed   😐 Meh   😑 Hard pass
```

To customize the wording/emoji:

```yaml
reaction:
  options:
    - id: "love"
      label: "😍 Obsessed"
    - id: "meh"
      label: "😐 Meh"
    - id: "skip"
      label: "❌ Hard pass"
```

- `id` — stored as the Sheet column value, keep stable once a post is live
- `label` — emoji + text shown on the button (component splits on the
  first space: emoji becomes the large glyph, rest becomes the caption)
- 2–4 options supported

**Position**: end of post, immediately before FAQ (not mid-content —
moved here from an earlier position, see Decisions Log in the handoff
memory if you're wondering why).

**Design**: dark header band (`#252220`) with a pulse-line icon, "REACT"
label, live reader count on the right. White card body below with the
option buttons.

### 6.2 Poll

**Only renders if `post.poll` is set.** No default — a poll needs an
authored question, there's no sensible fallback.

```yaml
poll:
  id: "unique-poll-id"
  question: "Your poll question?"
  options:
    - id: "option-a"
      label: "First option text"
    - id: "option-b"
      label: "Second option text"
```

- `id` — Sheet dedup key, must be unique per post
- `question` — shown as the card heading
- `options[].id` / `.label` — 2–4 options, `id` is the stored vote value

**Position**: ~50% mark, shares its slot with Quiz — **mutually
exclusive**. If a post has `quiz` set, quiz wins that slot and poll is
ignored even if also present. A post should only ever define one of the
two, not both.

**Design**: dark header band with a bar-chart icon, glowing red "LIVE"
dot (animated ping), "LIVE POLL" label, live vote count. After voting,
selected option's bar fills solid dark with white text; unselected options
get a faint fill. Long option labels truncate instead of colliding with
the % badge.

### 6.3 Quiz

**Only renders if `post.quiz` is set.** Fully author-defined — any number
of questions, any number of results, scoring logic entirely from your
`weights` values. One component handles both "which look are you"
(recommendation) and "is this right for you" (diagnostic) style endgames —
the difference is just how you write `results`, not a different component.

```yaml
quiz:
  id: "unique-quiz-id"
  title: "Quiz title shown at the top"
  questions:
    - id: "q1"
      question: "First question text?"
      options:
        - id: "q1_a"
          label: "Answer option A"
          weights: { result_id_1: 2 }
        - id: "q1_b"
          label: "Answer option B"
          weights: { result_id_2: 2 }
    - id: "q2"
      question: "Second question text?"
      options:
        - id: "q2_a"
          label: "Answer option A"
          weights: { result_id_1: 1, result_id_2: 1 }
        - id: "q2_b"
          label: "Answer option B"
          weights: { result_id_2: 2 }
  results:
    - id: "result_id_1"
      title: "Result One Title"
      description: "Full description shown on the result card."
      image: "/images/optional-result-image.jpg"
      ctaLabel: "Optional button text"
      ctaHref: "/optional/link"
    - id: "result_id_2"
      title: "Result Two Title"
      description: "Full description shown on the result card."
```

**How scoring works** (fully your control, nothing hardcoded):
1. Each answer option carries `weights: { resultId: number }` — how many
   points that answer contributes toward each result.
2. As the user answers, weights are summed per result id across all
   questions.
3. After the last question, the **highest-scoring result id wins**.
4. **Tiebreak**: if scores tie, the first result listed in your `results`
   array wins — array order = tiebreak priority.
5. An answer can contribute to multiple results at once (partial credit),
   e.g. `weights: { milky: 2, neutral: 1 }`.
6. Every `resultId` used in any `weights` object **must** match a real
   `id` in `results`, or that weight silently does nothing (no error).

**Position**: ~50% mark, same shared slot as Poll (quiz wins if both are
somehow set on the same post).

**Design**: dark header band with a sparkle icon, "QUIZ" label (switches
to "YOUR RESULT" once finished), question counter (`1 / 2`), animated
white progress bar that fills as questions are answered. Card height
auto-measures actual rendered content on every question/result change —
no hardcoded pixel value, so any number of questions/labels/description
lengths work without layout jitter.

