## 7. Author Matching

`resolveAuthor()` in `src/data/authors.ts` does **case-insensitive
substring matching** against the `author` frontmatter string:

```ts
if (lower.includes('jyoti') || lower.includes('jyotika'))
  return authors.find((a) => a.slug === 'jyoti-mirelle');

if (lower.includes('ri') || lower.includes('gaurav'))
  return authors.find((a) => a.slug === 'ri-mirelle');
```

**Confirmed working values** (all resolve correctly):
- `"ri-mirelle"` (slug)
- `"jyoti-mirelle"` (slug)
- `"Ri"` / `"Jyoti"` (display name)
- `"Gaurav Verma"` / `"Jyotika Verma"` (full name)

Any of these are safe to use in frontmatter — recommend `"ri-mirelle"` /
`"jyoti-mirelle"` (the slugs) for consistency with `authorPageUrl` and
image paths, which are also slug-keyed.

**⚠️ Real risk, not slug-vs-name**: the `"ri"` match is a **bare
substring**, not a whole-word match. Any author string containing "ri"
anywhere — `"Maria"`, `"Christina"`, `"Henri"`, etc. — will silently
misattribute to Ri. This isn't about which format you use; it'll happen
with slugs, display names, or full names alike if a future author's name
happens to contain "ri". If a third author is ever added, `resolveAuthor`
needs a tighter match (exact slug/name comparison, not `.includes()|`)
before that author is used in frontmatter.

**Silent failure**: if `author` doesn't match any known pattern,
`resolveAuthor` returns `undefined` and **AuthorCard simply doesn't
render** — no error, no warning, no visible gap. This already caused one
real bug in this build (an earlier version matched by slug against
full-name frontmatter and always returned nothing) — worth double-checking
after any change to this function.

### 7.1 Two separate `authors.ts` files — don't confuse them

- **`src/data/authors.ts`** — the static author array + `resolveAuthor()`
  (substring matching, described above). This is what
  `NailFeedTemplate.tsx` uses to decide whether/what to render in
  AuthorCard.
- **`src/lib/authors.ts`** — a *different* file. Builds author profile
  pages (`/authors/[slug]`) by scanning content directories for posts
  where `data.author === authorSlug`, using **exact string equality
  against the slug**, not substring matching.

**⚠️ Known gap**: `src/lib/authors.ts`'s `CONTENT_DIRS` list currently
covers `/blog`, `/nail-faqs`, `/work-nails`, `/spotlight`, `/topics`,
`/trend-reports`, `/business` — **it does not include
`src/content/nailfeed`**. This means Nail Feed posts render correctly on
their own page (via `resolveAuthor`'s substring match) but are currently
**invisible on author profile pages** — they won't count toward an
author's post list/count at `/authors/jyoti-mirelle` until Nail Feed is
added to `CONTENT_DIRS`. Not yet fixed as of this README.

Also note `getPostsByAuthor` requires an **exact** match on the slug
(`data.author === authorSlug`) — unlike `resolveAuthor`'s forgiving
substring match. This is a second, independent reason to always write the
slug (`"ri-mirelle"` / `"jyoti-mirelle"`) in frontmatter rather than a
full name: once the `CONTENT_DIRS` gap above is fixed, only the exact
slug will correctly attribute posts on author pages.

