## 8. Page Structure — Full Render Order

Current, confirmed order top to bottom:

1. ShareButton (floating)
2. Hero — category, H1, byline, date, 16:9 image
3. Breadcrumbs (`Home / Nail Feed / {title}`)
4. TableOfContents (mobile/tablet only — `block lg:hidden`, disappears at
   desktop widths; no desktop TOC exists)
5. WrapUp card (`tldr`) — only if set
6. Body, **part 1** (~33%)
7. **InlineNewsletter** — only if a second content part exists
8. Body, **part 2** (~33–67%)
9. **Poll or Quiz** (mutually exclusive, quiz wins) — only if a second
   content part exists and one of `poll`/`quiz` is set
10. **SocialFollowCTA** (all 5 platforms) — only if a third content part
    exists
11. Body, **part 3** (~67–100%) — only if it exists
12. **ReactionBar** — always renders
13. FAQ (`faqItems`) — only if present
14. FinalNewsletter (larger, name+email — distinct component from #7's
    compact InlineNewsletter)
15. AuthorCard — only if `author` resolves (see §7)
16. AboutEEAT
17. ReadMoreSection (related posts, capped at 6)

### How content splits into parts

Compiled HTML is split at `<h2>` boundaries closest to the 1/3 and 2/3
marks — **not** exact character/word math, and not /blog's exact 33/34/33.

- **3+ `<h2>`s**: full 3-part split, all mid-content slots render
  (newsletter → part 2 → poll/quiz → social → part 3)
- **Exactly 2 `<h2>`s**: only 2 parts exist — newsletter and poll/quiz
  both get their breaks, but the social CTA slot is skipped (there's no
  third break point for it to sit at without colliding)
- **0–1 `<h2>`s**: everything renders as one block — only the newsletter
  fallback logic applies, poll/quiz/social are all skipped since there's
  no break point at all

**Always write 3+ `<h2>` sections** per post — needed for full widget
placement (newsletter/poll-quiz/social all showing), a useful mobile TOC,
and even body pacing. Fewer than 3 headings means some mid-content slots
silently won't appear, which can look like a bug to whoever's reviewing
the post but isn't one.

